{
  "title": "AI calls fail with a confusing deserialization error when OpenRouter reports an upstream rate limit",
  "description": "Prod scrape job for https://japanesecooking101.com/whole-tomato-salad-recipe/ (2026-07-28) failed at enrich_auto_tag with: 'AI call failed: API error: APIError: Failed to parse JSON: unknown variant `error`, expected one of `stop`, `length`, `content_filter`, `tool_calls`, `null`'. \
The body was an HTTP 200 whose choice had finish_reason \"error\" and an embedded error object {code: 429, message: 'google/gemini-2.5-flash is temporarily rate-limited upstream...', metadata.error_type: rate_limit_exceeded}.\n\
\n\
openai-api-rs's FinishReason enum has no 'error' variant, so ramekin-core/src/ai/client.rs never sees the structured error. \
Users and logs get a serde message instead of 'upstream rate limited', and nothing distinguishes this transient failure from a real bug.\n\
\n\
Fix options: (a) check whether a newer openai-api-rs handles unknown finish reasons or OpenRouter's choice-level error, or (b) on this deserialization failure, parse the raw body for choices[].error and surface a clear AiError, for example AiError::RateLimited, with the provider message. \
Consider a bounded retry with backoff for rate_limit_exceeded, since the step otherwise needs a manual rerun. \
Don't cache the response (the existing code already avoids caching unusable responses; keep that true). \
Add a unit test with the captured response body.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "ai",
    "pipeline",
  ],
